WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:05.832
It is Sunday evening. There are four people to
feed, a

2
00:00:05.832 --> 00:00:10.329
busy week ahead, and a familiar question: what
are we cooking?

3
00:00:10.329 --> 00:00:14.827
Let's use Forkcast to plan three halal dinners,
start with what

4
00:00:14.827 --> 00:00:19.324
is already in the kitchen, and leave with one
useful shopping

5
00:00:19.324 --> 00:00:23.822
list. This is an example household, so you can
follow the

6
00:00:23.822 --> 00:00:24.640
whole journey.

7
00:00:43.551 --> 00:00:48.989
First, we need one dependable dinner. The recipe
collection includes real

8
00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:54.428
photographs, the original sources, and halal
notes. We will choose shakshuka.

9
00:00:54.428 --> 00:00:59.866
Open the details, read the ingredients, and
check the source before

10
00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:05.304
adding it to the plan. You can also search by
ingredient

11
00:01:05.304 --> 00:01:07.282
or filter by cuisine.

12
00:01:26.118 --> 00:01:31.009
Before choosing anything else, let's check the
cupboard. We have a

13
00:01:31.009 --> 00:01:35.899
short inventory note with rice, olive oil,
garlic, and eggs. Instead

14
00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:40.790
of typing every item, we can ask the image
extractor to

15
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:45.680
read the note. We are using a signed-in Codex
subscription for

16
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.569
this demonstration.

17
00:02:10.932 --> 00:02:15.661
The extractor has prepared the names and
quantities. Nothing has entered

18
00:02:15.661 --> 00:02:20.390
the pantry yet. This is our chance to correct an
amount

19
00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:25.119
or discard an item. Once the note matches what
we actually

20
00:02:25.119 --> 00:02:29.849
have, we save the reviewed items. Those
quantities will reduce the

21
00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.138
shopping list later.

22
00:03:03.071 --> 00:03:08.059
Someone in the family saved a Food Fusion pulao
video for

23
00:03:08.059 --> 00:03:13.047
the weekend. Let's bring its recipe into our
collection. The importer

24
00:03:13.047 --> 00:03:18.036
reads the available description or captions. A
pasted transcript is also

25
00:03:18.036 --> 00:03:23.024
available when the video service blocks access.
The model turns that

26
00:03:23.024 --> 00:03:25.291
material into an editable draft.

27
00:03:42.104 --> 00:03:46.980
Here is the imported draft. We can read the
ingredient amounts

28
00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.855
and instructions, check the original video, and
make any changes before

29
00:03:51.855 --> 00:03:56.731
saving. The source stays with the recipe. For
this family, we

30
00:03:56.731 --> 00:04:01.607
will use halal meat and keep the original
quantities visible for

31
00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:02.050
review.

32
00:04:24.325 --> 00:04:29.166
The third dinner is a family favorite: lemon and
chickpea rice.

33
00:04:29.166 --> 00:04:34.008
Personal recipes can start from an empty form,
or from a

34
00:04:34.008 --> 00:04:38.849
recipe note pasted here. We will preview our
note, then adjust

35
00:04:38.849 --> 00:04:43.690
the instructions. This recipe belongs to our
local household, so adding

36
00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.211
it does not change the shared recipe dataset.

37
00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:25.986
The recipe is saved. If we cook it differently
next time,

38
00:05:25.986 --> 00:05:30.542
we can edit it again. The ingredients are still
written in

39
00:05:30.542 --> 00:05:35.098
the form we will actually use: rice, cooked
chickpeas, lemon, garlic,

40
00:05:35.098 --> 00:05:39.655
olive oil, and a little salt. Now we have three
real

41
00:05:39.655 --> 00:05:41.311
choices for the week.

42
00:06:11.542 --> 00:06:15.996
Now let's give the assistant a useful job.
Prepare a meal

43
00:06:15.996 --> 00:06:20.450
plan with these three recipes. The assistant can
see the local

44
00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:24.904
collection and pantry, so we can ask in ordinary
language. It

45
00:06:24.904 --> 00:06:29.359
prepares the change for review; asking a
question does not give

46
00:06:29.359 --> 00:06:32.598
it permission to change everything in the
kitchen.

47
00:06:44.918 --> 00:06:49.103
The proposed plan lists the recipes it will
include. Read this

48
00:06:49.103 --> 00:06:53.287
before applying it. We are happy with the
choices, so we

49
00:06:53.287 --> 00:06:57.472
will apply the prepared change, then open the
planner to check

50
00:06:57.472 --> 00:07:01.656
the saved result. We can still edit the name or
dates

51
00:07:01.656 --> 00:07:04.319
and share the plan with the family.

52
00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.759
This is where the planning pays off. The active
plan becomes

53
00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:56.958
one shopping list, grouped by aisle. Compatible
quantities already in the

54
00:07:56.958 --> 00:08:02.157
pantry are deducted. We can ask the configured
model to improve

55
00:08:02.157 --> 00:08:07.356
ingredient interpretation, while the app keeps
the quantity calculations and source

56
00:08:07.356 --> 00:08:08.301
evidence explicit.

57
00:08:35.706 --> 00:08:40.418
Take a moment to read the result. Each item can
show

58
00:08:40.418 --> 00:08:45.130
the recipe lines it came from. Ingredient
insights help explain the

59
00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:49.842
names and pantry rules. Counts, weights, and
volumes stay separate when

60
00:08:49.842 --> 00:08:54.554
a conversion would be a guess. Any uncertain
amount stays visible,

61
00:08:54.554 --> 00:08:57.552
so we can check it before buying.

62
00:09:20.513 --> 00:09:25.631
We also have a few flyer offers to compare.
These stores

63
00:09:25.631 --> 00:09:30.749
and prices are fictional examples, clearly
labelled on the image. The

64
00:09:30.749 --> 00:09:35.867
image extractor reads the ingredient, pack size,
price, and currency. As

65
00:09:35.867 --> 00:09:40.984
with the pantry, we review the extracted offers
before saving them.

66
00:10:43.973 --> 00:10:48.670
The comparison buys whole packs and shows a
priced subtotal. It

67
00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:53.367
also lists ingredients with no recorded price.
That means this is

68
00:10:53.367 --> 00:10:58.064
not a promise about the cost of the whole
basket. Store

69
00:10:58.064 --> 00:11:02.761
suggestions rank the offers we entered. A
separate map search can

70
00:11:02.761 --> 00:11:06.604
find actual grocery stores near a location we
choose.

71
00:11:58.269 --> 00:12:02.852
At the shop, the same household is easy to use
on

72
00:12:02.852 --> 00:12:07.435
a phone-sized screen. Open the active list and
check off what

73
00:12:07.435 --> 00:12:12.018
goes into the basket. We can export a text copy,
share

74
00:12:12.018 --> 00:12:16.601
it, and save a shopping snapshot in history. The
saved snapshot

75
00:12:16.601 --> 00:12:20.350
remains useful even after our recipes or pantry
change.

76
00:12:46.045 --> 00:12:50.559
Here is the saved shopping trip, including the
items we collected.

77
00:12:50.559 --> 00:12:55.073
We can reopen or share it later. This part is a

78
00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:59.587
responsive browser demonstration of the
currently released app. It does not

79
00:12:59.587 --> 00:13:04.101
claim that a native phone build or disconnected
phone shopping has

80
00:13:04.101 --> 00:13:04.922
been tested.

81
00:13:20.032 --> 00:13:24.972
One last change: someone thinks we already have
yogurt. Let's ask

82
00:13:24.972 --> 00:13:29.912
the assistant to add it, but stop at the review.
If

83
00:13:29.912 --> 00:13:34.852
we have not checked the fridge, we should
discard the prepared

84
00:13:34.852 --> 00:13:39.793
change. That keeps an uncertain assumption out
of the pantry. The

85
00:13:39.793 --> 00:13:42.038
conversation remains available to revisit.

86
00:14:12.769 --> 00:14:17.469
We started with a busy week and a saved cooking
video.

87
00:14:17.469 --> 00:14:22.168
Now we have three dinners, a checked pantry, an
itemized shopping

88
00:14:22.168 --> 00:14:26.868
list, recorded offers, and a shopping history.
The artificial intelligence helped

89
00:14:26.868 --> 00:14:31.568
read and organize the information, and we stayed
in control of

90
00:14:31.568 --> 00:14:35.840
what was saved. That is a Sunday reset with
Forkcast.
